      "message": "1)\n\nThis tells the reporter process to exclude from the report any classes that were generated from source code in the current directory (because the current directory contains tests).\n\nI\u0027ll add a comment - unless you know of a better way to do it, in which case I\u0027ll do it your better way. What\u0027s here is the same as what\u0027s in Android.mk for jacoco_exclude (except that it uses \":\" as a separator)\n\n2) You\u0027re right. I suspect that in practice that it\u0027s not a problem, because that\u0027s the same thing that\u0027s done in Android.mk . I remember thinking this was odd myself, and then finding that there were cases where there were classes inside of other classes and that if I removed the \u0027*\u0027 then suddenly the inner classes were no longer excluded.",
